{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/pulls/3424","id":4278325569,"node_id":"PR_kwDOEFLz887_AhFB","html_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/pull/3424","diff_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/pull/3424.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/pull/3424.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/3424","number":3424,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Reject unknown OAuth client scopes at creation","user":{"login":"MsfPablo","id":129399053,"node_id":"U_kgDOB7Z5DQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/129399053?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MsfPablo","html_url":"https://github.com/MsfPablo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MsfPablo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MsfPablo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MsfPablo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MsfPablo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MsfPablo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MsfPablo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MsfPablo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MsfPablo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MsfPablo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Fixes #3406\n\n- [x] have read the [CONTRIBUTING.md](./CONTRIBUTING.md) file\n- [x] raised a GitHub issue or discussed it on the projects chat beforehand (#3406)\n- [x] added unit tests\n- [ ] added integration tests — the behaviour is fully covered at the `db.CreateOAuthClient` chokepoint every caller (CLI and v2 API) goes through; happy to add an `integration/cli_oauth_clients_test.go` case if you'd prefer one.\n- [ ] updated documentation if needed — the CLI `--scope` help text now also lists `users`, which was already part of the vocabulary\n- [x] updated CHANGELOG.md\n\n## Problem\n\n`CreateOAuthClient` validated tags via `validateACLTags` but not scopes: any string was deduplicated, sorted and stored verbatim, so `headscale oauth-client create -s 'EVIL:superuser' -s '../../etc/passwd'` succeeded. Since an unknown scope satisfies nothing in `scope.Grants`, this silently mints a client with fewer permissions than the operator asked for, and a typo like `auth_key` fails at request time rather than creation time.\n\n## Change\n\n- `scope.Scope.Valid()` reports membership in the existing `scope.Known()` vocabulary — the canonical list already used by the grant predicate, so validation cannot drift from enforcement.\n- `db.validateScopes` replaces the inline dedup/sort in `CreateOAuthClient`, rejecting unknown values with `ErrOAuthClientScopeInvalid` and an error naming the accepted set.\n- `mapError` maps that error to 400, so an invalid scope surfaces exactly like an invalid tag does today.\n- Validation lives in the db layer rather than the CLI so the v2 API path (`POST` keys) is covered too.\n\n## Verification\n\n```\ngo build ./...                       # clean\ngo vet ./...                         # clean\ngofmt -l .                           # no output\ngo test ./hscontrol/... ./cmd/...\n```\n\nTest suite is clean apart from two failures that also reproduce on an unmodified checkout in this environment: `TestAPIv2OAuthScopes` (needs `tofu`, provided by the nix dev shell) and `TestDialHeadscaleSocketRetriesUntilPresent` (macOS unix socket path length).\n\n---\nDisclosure: this patch was prepared with the assistance of Claude Code. I have reviewed the change and the test results above myself.","created_at":"2026-08-14T08:42:12Z","updated_at":"2026-09-25T19:24:38Z","closed_at":"2026-09-25T19:24:38Z","merged_at":"2026-09-25T19:24:38Z","merge_commit_sha":"d60bac5c79c55a060c910c8cf9989b6c4713756b","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[{"login":"nblock","id":131119,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzMTExOQ==","avatar_url":"https://ava